WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.089 --> 00:00:04.450
So we have some actual good news out of Israel
despite the fact that it may sort of take

00:00:04.450 --> 00:00:06.520
a while until anything really comes of this.

00:00:06.520 --> 00:00:11.290
And the news is that the longest serving prime
minister Benjamin Netanyahu has been indicted

00:00:11.290 --> 00:00:14.430
on charges of fraud, bribery and breach of
trust.

00:00:14.430 --> 00:00:21.910
Now, as many of you know, Netanyahu has been
a roadblock to any kind of serious peace possibilities

00:00:21.910 --> 00:00:27.610
in Israel for a very long time and not only
the, the, the not the only roadblock and the

00:00:27.610 --> 00:00:31.510
circumstances that present themselves there,
but a pretty massive one, particularly given

00:00:31.510 --> 00:00:36.470
his alliances with some of the most extreme
right wing elements in the Israeli Knesset.

00:00:36.470 --> 00:00:38.640
And he has now been indicted.

00:00:38.640 --> 00:00:44.680
This is the first prosecution in Israel of
a sitting prime minister and politically things

00:00:44.680 --> 00:00:46.810
in Israel are very hectic.

00:00:46.810 --> 00:00:50.910
There have been two inconclusive elections,
maybe going to a third vote.

00:00:50.910 --> 00:00:55.890
This has been going on for almost three years
with regard to possible charges against Netanyahu

00:00:55.890 --> 00:00:57.039
and the charges.

00:00:57.039 --> 00:01:02.770
Now finally, now the obvious question that
most people would ask is, well, what now does

00:01:02.770 --> 00:01:03.770
he leave?

00:01:03.770 --> 00:01:05.199
What happens next?

00:01:05.199 --> 00:01:06.199
It's unclear.

00:01:06.199 --> 00:01:09.020
This is widely uncharted territory for now.

00:01:09.020 --> 00:01:14.529
He can remain prime minister if convicted,
he would have to step down, but it could be

00:01:14.529 --> 00:01:18.479
three or even four years until a possible
conviction would happen.

00:01:18.479 --> 00:01:22.099
And that doesn't even account for the possibility
of appeals.

00:01:22.099 --> 00:01:26.849
So this really could be a very long time and
it's going to be more about financial, but

00:01:26.849 --> 00:01:30.900
I'm sorry, uh, not financial pressure, although
maybe so give it given the level of corruption

00:01:30.900 --> 00:01:35.509
he's allegedly involved in political pressure,
it may be more about political pressure, uh,

00:01:35.509 --> 00:01:37.869
in terms of actually making change happen.

00:01:37.869 --> 00:01:40.859
Netanyahu is apparently planning to stay for
the time being.

00:01:40.859 --> 00:01:45.599
He's immediately using it very Trumpy and
language to describe the entire thing.

00:01:45.599 --> 00:01:47.139
He's calling it a witch hunt.

00:01:47.139 --> 00:01:48.979
He's calling it an attempted coup.

00:01:48.979 --> 00:01:50.849
He wants the investigators investigated.

00:01:50.849 --> 00:01:55.799
I mean, it's a carbon Crow, a carbon copy
of the rhetoric that we've seen Donald Trump

00:01:55.799 --> 00:02:00.439
employ around investigations and allegations
into his misdeeds.

00:02:00.439 --> 00:02:04.229
But then there are also some pressing practical
political questions.

00:02:04.229 --> 00:02:08.929
Number one, Benjamin Netanyahu is a member
of the Likud party.

00:02:08.929 --> 00:02:14.200
Does the Likud party lose confidence in Netanyahu
and say he has to go?

00:02:14.200 --> 00:02:18.870
There are elements within the Likud party
that are saying we need a different leader,

00:02:18.870 --> 00:02:25.550
but so far the official position of Likud
has been, they're standing by Benjamin Netanyahu.

00:02:25.550 --> 00:02:30.569
What might the quickest way be to get Netanyahu
out?

00:02:30.569 --> 00:02:34.930
Probably if Likud says they're picking a different
leader, which they could do at any time, but

00:02:34.930 --> 00:02:38.480
again, right now it's not obvious that they're
going in that direction.

00:02:38.480 --> 00:02:44.459
If Benjamin Netanyahu stays in power, it would
not be surprising that he would try to get

00:02:44.459 --> 00:02:51.000
himself immunity through a congressional procedure
through the Israeli Knesset, but there is

00:02:51.000 --> 00:02:57.219
no Knesset right now in the sense that Benjamin
Netanyahu has not been able to form a government

00:02:57.219 --> 00:03:00.829
since the last election, so it is a complete
and total mess.

00:03:00.829 --> 00:03:05.859
What we do know, what we can say for sure
is that Netanyahu has been a disastrous prime

00:03:05.859 --> 00:03:12.950
minister from the point of view of moving
forward on peace and some kind of even steps

00:03:12.950 --> 00:03:16.689
towards breaking the impasse of the Israeli
Palestinian conflict.

00:03:16.689 --> 00:03:20.219
Now, every time I talk about this, if I don't
mention the both sides, somebody gets mad

00:03:20.219 --> 00:03:21.219
at me.

00:03:21.219 --> 00:03:26.790
There's no question that Hamas in Gaza has
also been a disgusting impediment to moving

00:03:26.790 --> 00:03:33.030
forward, but no matter that we still have
to point out that Benjamin Netanyahu has no

00:03:33.030 --> 00:03:38.689
credibility as an even potential arbiter of
peace and he has to go if we want a shot and

00:03:38.689 --> 00:03:41.769
hopefully that will be precipitated by this.

00:03:41.769 --> 00:03:42.769
Although we don't know.

00:03:42.769 --> 00:03:46.879
I've said before, Benjamin Netanyahu is allied
with the most extreme religious right-wing

00:03:46.879 --> 00:03:48.750
elements of the Israeli Knesset.

00:03:48.750 --> 00:03:53.760
That is not a group that is likely to oversee
any serious advancements in breaking the Israeli

00:03:53.760 --> 00:04:00.680
Palestinian conflict impasse there no credible
path to a lasting peace deal of any kind.

00:04:00.680 --> 00:04:05.819
As long as Benjamin Netanyahu is not only
there, but again under indictment on these

00:04:05.819 --> 00:04:07.060
charges.

00:04:07.060 --> 00:04:10.120
Israeli politics is complex, it's unpredictable.

00:04:10.120 --> 00:04:12.599
It's not obvious what the next step will be.

00:04:12.599 --> 00:04:19.400
Again, a conviction on these charges is unlikely
to be the fastest way to get him out, since

00:04:19.400 --> 00:04:25.300
it could take three to four years for an initial
conviction and then there can be appeals.

00:04:25.300 --> 00:04:26.680
So this is going to be a long one.

00:04:26.680 --> 00:04:29.110
The immediate news is of course good.

00:04:29.110 --> 00:04:33.620
We have to understand that this will be a
very slow process which might in the immediate

00:04:33.620 --> 00:04:38.970
change, very little or something could happen
like Likud saying Netanyahu's out, here's

00:04:38.970 --> 00:04:42.380
our new leader, which might actually bring
change more quickly.

00:04:42.380 --> 00:04:49.660
Uh, there is probably more to gain by trying
to seat a new government than trying to wait

00:04:49.660 --> 00:04:53.620
around for a Benjamin Netanyahu conviction.

00:04:53.620 --> 00:04:57.880
But some good news, although it's unclear
how quickly it will bring any change forward,

00:04:57.880 --> 00:04:58.129
we'll follow it for sure.

